  "implementation": "Reuse the existing curvature-from-derivatives implementation with explicit one-sided knot evaluation. Sample each active nonzero NURBS knot span independently and break strips at zero-speed samples. Persistent command state caches immutable source differentials by owner snapshots, tolerance and sampling options; scale/color edits share those arrays. Reuse native surface isocurve and NURBS trim producers in native builds, including trim-hole clipping. Paint in all viewport modes and expose scale, density, count, U/V and colors in a panel that persists while modeling. Direct panel display changes leave active point getters intact.",
  "display_scale": "Hair tip = point - curvature * 2^((Scale-100)/2). Native extracted circle graphs at scales 50,98,100,102,200 independently support this multiplier and outward sign. Scale and density tessellation are separate controls.",
  "sampling_policy": "8*2^Density intervals per nonzero knot span, with separate one-sided ends. Density 0..10. Surface Count 2..64 denotes evenly spaced stations including boundaries in each enabled axis. The aggregate station limit is 200000; checked size arithmetic rejects overflow before allocation. Global budget failures cannot expose stale flattened graphs on a later query. Display arithmetic must remain representable.",
