  "limits": [
    "The 153 common point/curvature samples agree within 1e-6. Native source construction uses the NURBS chart for ellipses, so local comparison samples use that same source-admission convention. Recipe geometry is the only producer input. The case named cubic contains an explicit rational quadratic definition.",
    "Native extracted envelope polylines are retained in full. Independent local knot-span sampling is not asserted to match native tessellation, hair placement, default colors or surface count/trim behavior. Circle-envelope relative errors test the display multiplier, not an absolute geometry tolerance at the extremely enlarged scale 200.",
    "Native captures cover curve graph commands and extraction. Surface/trim-hole behavior is tested locally with portable and native producers; complete native surface graph display parity is open. Transient transform/grip previews retain the prior comb until source acceptance. SubDs and persisted 3DM analysis metadata are not implemented.",
    "This is sampled display, not a continuous maximum-curvature or global extrema certificate. Singularities between stations may remain unresolved. Exact zero-speed sampled stations are omitted and counted; other numerical failures reject. No performance or new sanitizer qualification is claimed.",
    "The initial three-case native capture predates the additional unknown-command history guard. The final nine-case capture uses the current native probe. Both used the owned private headless launcher and public SDK/commands, restored graph settings, and retained source geometry. No Wine/FEX/license configuration or vendor source was changed.",
    "Historical hash values and nonhash metadata are preserved with immutable Git references. The pre-existing 69 unverifiable historical records remain untouched."
  ],
